WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:07.000
Groundwork 2.0 adds a Health page. Everything you'll see here belongs to a made-up sample household.

2
00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:13.946
Medical bills, your plan year, a health reserve and your HSA now sit together, on one page.

3
00:00:14.796 --> 00:00:21.025
A bill is kept exactly as the provider sent it. It becomes something you owe only when you say it's yours.

4
00:00:21.875 --> 00:00:27.870
When a card charge might be the same bill, Groundwork counts both until you say so. It never guesses.

5
00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:35.803
It shows which monthly amounts your own record can sustain. It never tells you what to offer, and it never contacts anyone.

6
00:00:36.653 --> 00:00:45.186
If a bill goes to collections, it stays here with its own running balance, never in your debt plan, and nothing is added that the collector didn't send.

7
00:00:46.036 --> 00:00:54.143
Your deductible and out-of-pocket maximum are shown as your insurer reports them. Groundwork never works them out from your spending.

8
00:00:54.993 --> 00:01:01.606
A health reserve is money set aside in an account you already have, aimed at the most a covered year can cost.

9
00:01:02.456 --> 00:01:09.496
Health spending is a record, not a budget. There's no limit to beat, and Groundwork never suggests spending less on care.

10
00:01:10.346 --> 00:01:17.471
Say whom care was for, payment by payment. The visit report and the year in review are ready to print when you need them.

11
00:01:18.321 --> 00:01:24.828
Names are labels, not locks, and the page says so plainly. You can hide Health from the sidebar at any time.

12
00:01:25.928 --> 00:01:30.600
And nothing about your health ever leaves your computer. Groundwork 2.0 is free.
